          %p
            A subfunctor
            %math#mathml_627003cea389e0c4b676ceb1edfe99a3e9e4f2b4_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\subseteq X
            is called
            %em open subfunctor
            resp.
            %em closed subfunctor
            if for every transformation
            %math#mathml_627003cea389e0c4b676ceb1edfe99a3e9e4f2b4_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u:T\to X
            we have
            %math#mathml_627003cea389e0c4b676ceb1edfe99a3e9e4f2b4_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi u
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^{-1}(Y)
            is of the form
            %math#mathml_627003cea389e0c4b676ceb1edfe99a3e9e4f2b4_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
